-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Choice of Law (Limitation Periods) Act 1993`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- A Gregorian leap year.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF m EQUALS 2
        THEN IF `leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
        IF (m EQUALS 4) OR (m EQUALS 6) OR (m EQUALS 9) OR (m EQUALS 11)
        THEN 30
        OTHERWISE 31

-- The day a number of whole years and months after a day: the same day of the month, in the month that many years and
-- months on; where that month has no such day (29 February in a common year, 31 April), the last day of that month
-- (fork F6).
GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the months` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` `the years` `years and` `the months` `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` `the month reached` `the year reached`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS `the months` PLUS (`the years` TIMES 12)
        `the month reached` MEANS (`the months counted` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the year reached` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS ((`the months counted` MINUS (`the months counted` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the number of days in month` `the month reached` `of` `the year reached`
            THEN `the number of days in month` `the month reached` `of` `the year reached`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`
